      "pronunciationText": "Last video, we put one function inside another. Now let's multiply two of them, the way a deck's area is its length times its width. Here's e to the x, here's sine x, and here's their product, e to the x sine x. A quick guess for its derivative: just multiply the two derivatives. That gives e to the x times cos x. At pi over two, cos x is zero, so the guess says the curve is flat there. But look at the curve. At pi over two, it's climbing steeply. So how do both factors really contribute to the slope?"
    },
