      "outputTokens": 1157,
      "costUsd": 0.010503,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's why that guess fails, with the deck. It's four metres long and two metres wide, so its area is eight square metres. While it's being built, its length grows by one metre a day, and its width by half a metre a day. Multiply those two rates, and you'd guess the area grows by half a square metre a day. Now watch it grow. The extra length adds a strip down the side, two metres long: one metre a day, times two metres, is two square metres a day. The extra width adds a strip along the top, four metres long: half a metre a day, times four metres, is another two square metres a day. So right now, the area grows at four square metres a day, eight times the guess. Each side's growth is multiplied by the other side's size."
    },
